{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And he set it up for a pillar</b> — Our Sages have already explained (Avodah Zarah 53) the difference between the pillar (matzevah) and the altar (mizbeach): the pillar is a single stone and the altar is many stones. And it further appears that the pillar is made for pouring a libation of wine upon it and for pouring oil upon it, not for burnt offering and not for sacrifice, while the altar is for offering upon it burnt offerings and peace offerings. And when they came into the land, the pillar was forbidden to them (Deuteronomy 16:22), because the Canaanites had set it up for themselves as a statute more than the altars — even though it is written of them (Exodus 34:13), 'you shall tear down their altars' — or perhaps He did not wish to forbid everything and left the altar, which is suitable for libations and for sacrifices:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:36:17.800873213Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}